\itemize{
\item \strong{No \code{seed}.} The same refusal as \code{\link[=pf_round_sample]{pf_round_sample()}}, for the same
reason: an assignment that cannot be redealt cannot be audited, and these
labels outlive the session that dealt them.
\item \strong{No population fingerprint.} \code{grant_id} is positional, and a CSV does
not carry attributes -- so a draw read back from \code{ADJ-ROUND-STAGE1.csv}
has lost its fingerprint and must be given one. Labels dealt without it
cannot be re-attached to anything later.
\item \strong{An overlap with \code{k = 1}.} There is no second labeler to be the second
opinion, so the request is not a small overlap; it is none.
\item \strong{A duplicated \code{grant_id}.} One case in two shards by accident is the
overlap arriving unmarked, which is the one thing it must not be.
